  "ingredients": [
    "4 medium zucchini",
    "1 1/2 cup blackberries",
    "2 teaspoon ground cinnamon",
    "2 tablespoon lemon juice",
    "1/3 cup powdered erythritol",
    "2 teaspoon cream of tartar",
    "1 1/2 cup almond flour",
    "2 tablespoon erythritol",
    "3 tablespoon butter",
    "1 teaspoon vanilla extract",
    "1/2 cup heavy cream (whipped)"
  ],
  "instructions": [
    {
      "text": "Measure out and prepare all the ingredients. Preheat oven to 350F.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-blackberry-zucchini-crumble/#wprm-recipe-53569-step-0-0",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2020/11/Keto-Blackberry-Apple-Crumble-1.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cut off the ends of the zucchini and peel them. Slice the zucchini in half lengthwise and scoop out the seeds with a spoon. Discard the seeds.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-blackberry-zucchini-crumble/#wprm-recipe-53569-step-0-1",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2020/11/Keto-Blackberry-Apple-Crumble-2.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Chop the zucchini into small pieces. Add the chopped zucchini into a pan of boiling water for 2-3 minutes. Drain and pat dry.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-blackberry-zucchini-crumble/#wprm-recipe-53569-step-0-2",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2020/11/Keto-Blackberry-Apple-Crumble-3.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "In a bowl, combine cooked zucchini, blackberries, cinnamon, lemon juice, powdered erythritol, and cream of tartar. Mix until fully combined.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-blackberry-zucchini-crumble/#wprm-recipe-53569-step-0-3",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2020/11/Keto-Blackberry-Apple-Crumble-4.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "In another bowl, combine almond flour, erythritol, and vanilla extract. Press the butter into the other ingredients using a fork to make a crumble like consistency.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-blackberry-zucchini-crumble/#wprm-recipe-53569-step-0-4",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2020/11/Keto-Blackberry-Apple-Crumble-5.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "In an oven-safe skillet, add the blackberry zucchini filling to the bottom of the pan. Then sprinkle with the crumble topping. Bake for 30-40 minutes, or until topping is golden brown.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-blackberry-zucchini-crumble/#wprm-recipe-53569-step-0-5",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2020/11/Keto-Blackberry-Apple-Crumble-6.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "In a separate bowl, whip the cream until desired consistency is reached. Top the crumble with whipped cream and enjoy warm!",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-blackberry-zucchini-crumble/#wprm-recipe-53569-step-0-6",
      "imageSource": null
    }
  ],
